  "result": "Perfect! All **419 tests pass** (404 existing + 15 new dashboard tests).\n\n## Dashboard Implementation Summary\n\n**Added: `src/reports.js` - `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function**\n\nReturns a comprehensive dashboard object with:\n- **`counts`**: Object with invoice counts by status\n  - `draft`, `issued`, `partially_paid`, `paid`\n- **`outstanding`**: Total amount still due (sum of balances on issued and partially_paid invoices)\n- **`overdue`**: Object with overdue metrics\n  - `count`: Number of overdue invoices\n  - `amount`: Total amount overdue\n- **`topCustomers`**: Array of top 3 customers by amount due\n  - Sorted highest to lowest\n  - Format: `[{ customerId, due }, ...]`\n\n**New Tests: `test/reports.test.js`** (15 test cases)\n- Count invoices by status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Calculate outstanding amount correctly\n- Outstanding only includes issued and partially_paid invoices\n- Overdue metrics are calculated correctly\n- Top customers ranking and sorting\n- Top customers exclude fully paid invoices\n- Top customers handle partially paid invoices\n- Handle fewer than 3 customers gracefully\n- Mixed invoice statuses\n- All required fields present\n- Data structure validation\n\n**Key Implementation Details:**\n- Counts all invoices categorized by their status\n- Outstanding sums `balanceDue()` for unpaid invoices only\n- Uses existing `overdueInvoices()` for overdue calculations\n- Groups unpaid invoices by customer and sums amounts due\n- Returns top 3 customers sorted by amount due descending\n- Returns fewer than 3 customers if not enough data",
